<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="resources">
    <title>Additional Resources</title>
    <p>
        Your first resource is your instructor's help hours! Here are a few more resources for when your instructor is not around.
    </p>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Tutoring</title>
        <p>
            Green River College students can get free tutoring at the Math Learning Center on campus in Cedar Hall 313. Information about the hours of operation can be found
            at the <url href="https://www.greenriver.edu/students/academics/tutoring-resources/math-learning-center/index.html" visual="Math Learning Center's webpage"/>.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Textbooks</title>
        <p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <url href="https://openstax.org/details/books/prealgebra-2e" visual="Openstax Prealgebra 2e"/> (Seasons 1-6)
                    </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                    <p>
                        <url href="https://openstax.org/details/books/prealgebra-2e" visual="Openstax Elementary Algebra 2e"/> (Seasons 7-10)
                    </p>
                
                </li>
            </ul>
            Both available for free online.
        </p>
         </paragraphs>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Calculators</title>
            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            This guide utilizes the free GeoGebra calculator, which you can access using the calculator icon at the top of the page.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Another excellent, free online calculator is the <url href="https://www.desmos.com/" visual="Desmos Calculator"/>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Another free online calculator and the best free calculator app for your phone is the <url href="https://www.numworks.com/" visual="Numworks Calculator"/>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </paragraphs>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>YouTube Channels</title>
        <p>
            A couple of good YouTube channels for math review are:
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <url href="https://www.youtube.com/@TheOrganicChemistryTutor/playlists" visual="The Organic Chemistry Tutor"/>
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <url href="https://www.youtube.com/@ProfessorLeonard/courses" visual="Professor Leonard"/>
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</section>